Read CLAUDE.md (including the new "Grading budget" section), PLAN.md (Phase 6) and your agent definition; they are binding.

**Measurements by the integrator:**
- The grader's fuel limit is 500M wasm instructions per frame (`fuel_per_frame` in grader.yaml). Phase 6 needs at least 2x headroom, so every graded test must run with no trap at **250M**.
- Today **varooom-3d-gameplay traps at 250M**: video 0.989 becomes 0.046. spout and heartwrench do not trap at 250M.
- Native ms/frame (release, with replay inputs): spout 16.2, varooom 13.3, piugba 11.0, heartwrench 10.6, chip-advance 9.8, all others under 9.
- How to check fuel, as the integrator did:
  - build a subset corpus dir whose grader.yaml sets `fuel_per_frame: 250000000`;
  - run the docker grader on it;
  - look for "run_frame trap" in the log.
  - Example: `/tmp/claude-1000/-var-www-html-test-projects-gba-trial-gba-emu/ec739230-fb4b-467b-9709-e53c38e370f4/scratchpad/fuel250000000/` (sub/ is the corpus, log.txt the output; the command pattern is `docker run --rm -v $GBA_EVAL:/repo:ro -v <sub>:/subset -v $GBA_EVAL/corpus/roms:/subset/roms:ro -v $GBA_EVAL/corpus/replays:/subset/replays:ro -v $GBA_EVAL/corpus/reference-cache:/subset/reference-cache:ro -v <dir>:/p -w /repo gba-eval-grader /p/cand.wasm /subset/ /p/out`).
  - Wrap every grader run in `flock /tmp/gba-emu-grader.lock`.
- Native profiling is free and unlimited: `perf` if installed, or timing a native replay runner. The integrator's runner is at `.../scratchpad/replayer/` (usage: `replayer <rom> <replay.txt> <frames> <outdir>`).

**Hot paths you may change:**
- `src/cpu/mod.rs` (step, fetch, halt), `src/cpu/arm.rs`, `src/cpu/thumb.rs` (decode dispatch);
- `src/bus.rs` (read/write/charge);
- `src/io.rs` (dispatch);
- `src/ppu/*.rs` (line rendering, compositor, sprites, affine);
- `src/apu/*.rs` (mixer and PSG step);
- `src/timer.rs`, `src/dma.rs`;
- `src/gba.rs` (`run_frame` / `advance_components` loop).
For `src/lib.rs`, add the test only. Don't change ABI behaviour.

**Hard rule: behaviour must not change.** Every graded score must stay within 0.005 of the phase-5 milestone (`results/milestones/phase-5/summary.json`). Optimise the representation, not the semantics. Also no allocation on hot paths, and keep the code readable per CLAUDE.md.

**Also add the reset-determinism test** (PLAN.md Phase 6): load a ROM, run 100 frames, `emu_reset()`, run 100 frames, then compare framebuffer hashes, and audio too if cheap. It must pass. emu_reset must produce exactly the same state as emu_load_rom. Look for state that survives reset: globals, the lib.rs buffers, anything outside `Gba`. Put it in lib.rs `#[cfg(test)]` or tests/. If no test ROM is available in-repo, use one from $GBA_EVAL/corpus/roms/ via an absolute path and skip gracefully if it is missing.

**Grading budget (CLAUDE.md):** at most 5 grader runs in total, all serialised with flock. Plan them as:
- 1 baseline at 250M on all replays;
- up to 2 checks while optimising;
- 1 final full-suite run at the normal 500M limit for the "within 0.005" check;
- 1 final 250M no-trap check.
Then commit your best version and report.

Report the commits; native ms/frame before and after per replay; the 250M trap result before and after; full-suite scores versus phase-5; and the determinism test. ($GBA_EVAL=/var/www/html/test-projects/gba-eval)

